+Lojban Machine Grammar, EBNF Version, Final Baseline
+<p>This EBNF document is explicitly dedicated to the public domain by its =
author, The Logical Language Group, Inc. Contact that organization at: 2904=
 Beau Lane, Fairfax VA 22031 USA 703-385-0273 (intl: +1 703 385 0273)</p>
 <p>Explanation of notation: All rules have the form:</p>
 <div class=3D"c2">name<sub>number</sub> =3D bnf-expression</div>
 <br />
 <br />
 which means that the grammatical construct =93name=94 is defined by =93bnf=
-expression=94. The number cross-references this grammar with the rule numb=
ers in the YACC grammar. The names are the same as those in the YACC gramma=
r, except that subrules are labeled with A, B, C, ... in the YACC grammar a=
nd with 1, 2, 3, ... in this grammar. In addition, rule 971 is =93simple_ta=
g=94 in the YACC grammar but =93stag=94 in this grammar, because of its fre=
quent appearance.
 <ol>
 <li>Names in lower case are grammatical constructs.</li>
 <li>Names in UPPER CASE are selma'o (lexeme) names, and are terminals.</li=
>
 <li>Concatenation is expressed by juxtaposition with no operator symbol.</=
li>
 <li>| represents alternation (choice).</li>

